Answers local counsel on “local representative” (24.04.2023)



_The answers in the questionnaire indicate that Bolt must notify the Data Protection Authority (DPA) before collecting and processing personal data of passengers and drivers. We are currently preparing the necessary paperwork for the notification procedure (Articles 35-38) based on the template provided by the Angolan Data Protection Authority (APD)._

_According to Article 3(4), it is mandatory for companies not established in Angola to designate a local representative, who must also be listed in the notification form._



_This leads me to the following questions:_

 

Appointment of a local representative:

# _Are we correct in assuming that in our case it is mandatory to appoint a local representative?_  {color:#4c9aff}*ADCA:  Yes, you are*{color}{color:#4c9aff}*_._*{color}  _Can a local law firm take on this role?_  {color:#4c9aff}*ADCA:  Yes it can*{color}{color:#4c9aff}*_._*{color}

_1.2. Does the local representative serve only as the first point of contact or are there other rights/obligations connected with this function?_  {color:#4c9aff}*ADCA:  The local representative will not just serve only as the first point of contact. There are other rights/obligations connected with this function, namely, as per indicated in the Law:*{color}{color:#4c9aff} *_“The Representative shall substitute the Principal in all of his/her rights and obligations (without prejudice to his/her own liability) in relation to data processing._*{color}

_1.3. What annual costs can be expected for the appointment of a local law firm as local representative?_ {color:#4c9aff}*_ADCA: This will vary depending on the law firm, since each law firm will estimate it’s own costs based on how much they consider the risk associated with the rights/obligations above are valued._*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_ADCA’s proposal for such services:_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_i)          We propose an annual fee of $5.000;_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_ii)          A fixed fee of $1.000 per notification – it is presumably to have notifications only on three occasions, namely:_*{color}

* {color:#4c9aff}*When starting the data processing;*{color}
* {color:#4c9aff}*Every two years;*{color}
* {color:#4c9aff}*When the goal of the data processing is to be change, and the Data Protection Agency must be notified;*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_iii)         In the event of penalties, Bolt should make the payment within the estipulate period by the Data Protection Agency. If not, we will advance the amount, but Bolt should reimburse it with an additional 25%, plus the Fixed rate of Euribor at the time of the celebration of the EL._*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_Please note that:_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_i)          The above amounts don´t include VAT;_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_ii)          The above amounts don´t include any fees to be paid to third parties;_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_iii)         The above amounts don´t include bank transfers;_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_iv)         The above amounts are strictly for the representation;_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_v)         The above proposal must be concluded through a EL._*{color}

# Duration of the notification process

{color:#4c9aff}*_Article 35(2) states that in the case of a mere notification, the data protection authority must make a decision within thirty days of receipt of the controller's request._*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_Is it possible to start data processing after/with the submission of the documents or is it advisable to wait for a positive response in the notification procedure (especially in view of the possible sanctions; Article 35 in conjunction with Article 51(1) lit a 2, Article 51(2))?  ADCA: According to the Law, in cases where mere notification is required, data processing can only start in one of the following situations, with prior notification to the Agency (which is equivalent to saying: "after/with the submission of the documents"):_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_i)          if the Agency gives a positive opinion on the notification (within the thirty day period); or_*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_ii)          if the Agency does not reply within thirty days counted from the notification (since if the Agency does not reply, the Law considers that the processing has been duly notified)._*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*_Therefore, it is not possible to start data processing after/with the submission of the documents, and it is necessary to wait until the earlier of:_*{color}

* {color:#4c9aff}*a positive reply from the Agency; or*{color}
* {color:#4c9aff}*expiry of thirty days, counted from the date of notification (in case of no reply from the Agency).*{color}

