Here are the result of my investigation on this task, was part of the duty. This crash only happens on pre-live, no live crashes were reported according to *Crashlytics*. The crash report from [*Crashlytics dashboard*|https://console.firebase.google.com/project/taxify-client/crashlytics/app/android:ee.mtakso.client.preLive/issues/2db4b1cd5b1bfd28340435ec197e7630?time=last-thirty-days&sessionEventKey=643E6DFD0087000162B6861CBBDB1AE2_1801777422713187055&subIssues=f9294fd36a2023c9ae4d7fa32618e495] indicates

{noformat}AppCompatSpinner{noformat}

Please see the report for the details. The indicated view component is only used in the view where feature flags are managed and that view is only visible on pre-live. [~accountid:632dba2c61dbef2805be2e6c] also confirmed that she experienced this only on pre-live. Probably the main reason is the {{@+id/spinner}} of the {{AppCompatSpinner}} in the {{item_feature_flag.xml}} is not unique. For example, {{rib_choose_location_on_map_bs.xml}} has a view with the same id. Thus, having id collisions causing the {{ClassCastException}}  in the event of {{onRestoreInstanceState}} when trying the set a state that belongs to a view of different type. I have tried to re-produce it for many times but I was unable to. However, since the crash is pre-live only and it is low frequency, we agreed to skip any further investigation for now and moving the ticket to the backlog. [~accountid:632dba2c61dbef2805be2e6c] [~accountid:61f105a9cb7c5f006bf067fb]

